<h1>Questions and answers</h1>

<section class="faq">

<h2 id="what">What is RoomXDynamics?</h2>
<p>RoomXDynamics is an iPhone app in development. It simulates a section through a room with an outside wall and a window. It shows, qualitatively, how warm and cool air move in the model and how cool the wall surface gets.</p>

<h2 id="language">What language is the app in?</h2>
<p>German and English. The app follows the language of your iPhone: German if your iPhone is set to German, otherwise English.</p>

<h2 id="available">Can I download it?</h2>
<p>Not yet. RoomXDynamics is in development and not yet available in the App Store.</p>

<h2 id="results">What do the results show?</h2>
<p>Trends in the model, made for comparing settings. The air movement is a two-dimensional flow simulation; the wall surface temperature comes from steady heat conduction with common design values. The <a href="/method/">method</a> page lists what the model includes and leaves out.</p>

<h2 id="measure">Does the app take measurements?</h2>
<p>No. RoomXDynamics calculates from the inputs you choose, such as outside temperature, window and wall.</p>

<h2 id="mould">Does it tell me whether a wall will get mould?</h2>
<p>No. It shows how cold and damp the wall surface gets in the model, as a risk estimate in three levels with a range. Room corners and walls behind furniture are usually colder. If you can see mould: have the wall looked at on site by a professional.</p>

<h2 id="price">Is there a price yet?</h2>
<p>The price has not been set.</p>

<h2 id="privacy">Does this website track me?</h2>
<p>No. This website has no cookies, no analytics and no tracking. Details are in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2 id="audience">Who is it for?</h2>
<p>People who furnish, renovate or design their home and want to see, in a model, how warm and cool air moves in a room and how cool its walls get. It shows a model room, not a copy of yours.</p>

</section>
